    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `getOwner` response needed a computed `initials` field (e.g. `\"J.S.\"` for John Smith). Since `OwnerDto` is generated from `openapi.yml` and `displayName` was already handled the same way, I followed that established pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `initials` via a small `initials(owner)` default method mirroring the existing `displayName(owner)`, with a private `initial(name)` helper that upper-cases the first character and appends a dot. This keeps the name-formatting logic in one place and avoids duplicating the per-name logic.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` passes (`john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`), and the build is green.",
